+### What `met=True` does not show (round-49 wave attacks)
+
+- **Disclosed before the wave** (`.ufo/waves/round-49/preregistration.json`, `limits` — not wave findings): C1 witnesses that the frozen binary executed as the listener with the frozen model and that its tokenizer answered a counter nonce; it does not show the binary came from the downloaded archive at replay time (the round-48 replay leg's digest checks carry that), and a replay that runs the same binary from a host copy still passes the witness. The exe check reads `/proc/<pid>/exe`, so it is Linux-only and fails closed on a process the counter cannot read. C2's origin is the text's first appearance in the file, so a line born in the head, later carried in a dated section and deleted from the head again stays ungraded, and identical text born in both places counts as exempt-born. C2's lane leg bounds the tool's ungraded count by the counter's own natively-exempt count per event; it does not recompute eligibility or the held measures, and the sub-20 threshold is unchanged.
+- **C1, wave findings.** Seat K1Cheat: two shortcuts still reach `witness=1 cap=1 newrow=1 witnessed=3/3 met=True` — a decoy replay that never re-runs the lifecycle (it downloads and digest-checks the inputs, then serves the witness from a server it starts itself) and an environment-injection hijack of the pristine build tree; the witness proves a frozen-binary server was alive, not that the replay tool ran it. Seat K1Design: the witness does not bind the observed server to the process whose captures the rerun receipt holds, nor the model bytes the server loaded (the `-m` argument hashes, the loaded file need not); three corrections specified for the next counter (pid/port from the rerun receipt, start time, the model path the process maps). Seat X1Timeout: the timeout path is bounded and tears down with `witness.released=false`, but a stale `release` left in the witness directory yields `released=true, waited_ms=0` with no observation window, and a harness failure mid-witness is reported as a comparison difference (exit 1) instead of a refusal (exit 2). Seat X1Compat: the witness block is additive and not compared; the round-47 C2 counter and the round-48 v5 counter both still pass, and a witness directory that already holds `release` is the same zero-window risk (R-1). Seat U1Prior: the witness is a local, unsigned observer-nonce background check (RFC 9334 sense) — kernel measurement of the running image plus reference-value appraisal, with no build provenance and no nonce-to-binary binding, as the preregistration concedes. Seat R1Provenance: all four frozen constants (server digest, model URL and digest, README commit) match the outside world. Seat K1Fresh: a fresh session can run a witnessed replay from `SKILL.md` and the two `--help` pages, but `SKILL.md` names no witness, so the how-to line is an integration item. Seat X1Record: a new v5 receipt recorded against the real b11909 archive replays with `match=True` and a second witnessed record was observed from 